Brian Wallingford  <brian@meganet.net> wrote:
> Hello,
>
> Just built a new 2.0.35 kernel on an LX164 with NCR53C875 ultra SCSI3
> controller.  On booting, I get:
>
> VFS:Cannot open root device 08:02 , followed, of course, by:
> Kernel panic:  VFS: Unable to mount root fs on 08:02

This error is generally caused by having the wrong SCSI configuration
in the kernel, or you forgot to include SCSI disk support in the kernel.

Make sure you compiled both into the kernel and not just as a module,
unless you have the modules also in an initrd.

> Now the strange part:  I've verified that 08:02 corresponds to the
> correct root partition (/dev/sda2) and I can boot into the old 2.0.34
> kernel without a problem.  I have configured support for ext2 into the
> new kernel.
>
> Any ideas?


