: Hello all,
Hello!

: I recently purchased a AXPPci33 Alpha motherboard with a 21066 166mhz
: CPU. 
: I installed redhat 5.1 on the 1gb scsi disk with no problems. Then I
: rebooted, and from the SRM console, I booted the MILO disk I had inthe
: drive. Now after MILO loads, I type:
: boot sd0:vmlinuz.gz root=/dev/sda2
: and it starts to boot and after it says:
: Partition Check
: (dumps the partitions)
: it says kernel not found.
MILO follows the same device/partition scheme that Linux does, i.e. first
SCSI disc is sda and partitions are sda1 and following.
After RH install the kernel can be found on your _root_ partition. You can
check the kernel's name using MILO's "ls" command, i.e. with
  ls sda2
if sda2 is your root drive.
Then try
  boot <root-device>:/<kernel-name>

: Please help!
: thanks,
