In article <6umk1u$o60$1@horn.wyoming.com>, Hal Nash <hnash@wyoming.com>wrote:
> I just got RedHat 5.1 installed.   My linux book says that I need to edit
> the inittab file to make X windows come up automatically.  But it doesn't
> say how to edit it.

/etc/inittab

Look for the line that looks like:

id:3:initdefault:

Change the '3' to a '5' for the box to default into init level 5, which
fires up the xdm login manager.

The reason they don't tell you what to change it to is because different
distributions of Linux (hell, different flavors of Unix and Unix-like OSs)
have different things in different run-levels.

> I looked for emacs...couldn't find it.  Isn't that what I need to edit the
> file?

You can use emacs, vi, pico, joe, jove, ed, ex, perl, sed, or any other text
editor.

