Terran,

I feel your pain. I just went through this one myself on a Compaq Proliant
5000 server this year. The problem lies in your not being able to probe for
interfaces when you have more than one of them. I remember reading why this
was a problem, but have since forgoten why.

The long and the short of it is that if you are using NE2000 clones, you are
going to fave to find some way to set and save their configurations so you
can explicitly refrence their locations in either the boot parameters or the
kernel config file. Only after you can get a successfully saved compatable
setup on both cards will it boot up fine and recognize them both.

