Hi, 
	I have the same configuration as you're trying to set up - 1 ethernet
card connected to a DSL line, the other to an internal network. I have
an 486, not an alpha, but I this will help you anyway.
This is what I did : 
1.got isapnptools
2.ran isapnpdump to generate the file /etc/isapnp.conf
3.edited the /etc/isapnp.conf file to choose interrupts and addresses
(shown below)
4.ran isapnp /etc/isapnp.conf
5.loaded the ethernet driver modules by doing :
