To solve the power problem on the internal SCSI hard drive, I took a
old broken power supply at snipped of a cable that had a floppy
connector and a hard drive connector on the same run.  I used the
floppy connector to connect to the controller card and the hard drive
connector (of course) to connect to the hard drive.  It was a tight
fit for the floppy connector and the pins bent a bit, but it was
secure.  I can't remember what the pinout was, but I looked at the
manual I downloaded and was able to tell from the black and white
picture where the yellow (light grey in the B/W picture) was.  Let me
know if you can't figure it out and I'll break open my computer and
take a look.

