juhana paavola <hgm@saunalahti.fi> wrote:
: Why my S3 card in Alpha XL266 doesn't give 16bit color modes ?
: Only I have runned is 8bit modes ,but I need the 16bit too.
: Card has 2mb memory and it worked in intel machine fine.
: Alpha is running RH 5.1 and intel too.
What does happen if you start X at 16bpp?
Do you get something like "No screens found"?
Then you might have a wrong X server. Try updating the appropriate server
package. The reason is that egcs optimizes the kernel in another way than
gcc did and that this causes the kernel ro report other values to the X
server than it expects. This is fixed in newer X releases (for me
XFree86-SVGA-3.3.2.3-18 runs fine with a S3 Virge).
