>
>I'm having a somewhat similar problem - but I can ftp between my mac and
>my multia at a reasonable speed, about 100k/sec (slow, but useful). when i
>try to ftp between my multia and solaris, it's _really_ slow - about 15
>k/sec. i can ftp betwen solaris and the mac at normal speed - 800+k/sec.
>
>do i just need to install a newer ftpd, or something? this is kind of
>annoying, i have several hundred megabytes to transfer between the two.

Check your name service.

RedHat's FTP is set up to do a reverse lookup on the connecting
machines, so if you don;t have that machine in a DNS with a reverse
lookup table or in a hosts file, it will take a long time
to connect.

Zebee
