IIRC, there is no Netscape Communicator released specifically for
Linux/Alpha.  You'll have to either run the OSF/1 (Digital UNIX)
version, or you'll have to install EM86 and run one of the Linux/Intel
versions.  If your site has an OSF/1 or Digital UNIX site-license,
grab the libraries off an Alpha and run the OSF/1 Netscape (this is a
FAQ; I think it's on azstarnet somewhere).  If you can't obtain a copy
of these libraries, you'll have to use EM86.  I have no idea as to
what it takes to get EM86 up and going.  I've got it installed on my
file server (an AS200), but I never really used it.

