Hi:
I got mine from onsale too.
I assume your hardware had no problem.
Tell you my experience:
1. download rawrite.exe and udbudp38.img    from Digital.
2.rawrit this img file to a new disk.
3. insert this disk to your box and boot. it will      upgrade itself<or useF2>
4.Prepare 3 dos-formated disks.
5.copy linload.exe and Udb-nona from redhat    cdrom to one of these disks.(in
redhat cdrom 1 "milo" subdir)
6. use rawrite.exe (from redhat cdrom) to     creat your boot disk and
ramdisk(must fit     your machine)
7.change your boot selection to:
LOADIDENTIFIER=Linux SYSTEMPARTITION=multi (0)disk(0)fdisk(0)
OSLOADER=multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)\linload.exe
...
OSLOADFILENAME=\Udb-nona
OSLOADOPTIONS=
8.when you see:
milo>boot floppy
.....
boot:Linux
......
8.follow the message showed on your screen to insert boot disk or ramdisk.
9.Good luck.

