But it counts if you have 56 Megs (24+32) or 32 Megs. There are Multias with
500 MB ether, but 340 Megs should be enough when you strip Linux a bit (not
including all Window managers, etc.)

BTW: There are FOUR Alpha Versions of the "Multia" (and one? Intel). Two of
them use 2.5" Drives and two of them include a 3.5" Drive. The 3.5" Drives
don't have a PCI Slot.

Due to power restrictions (12V is very weak) , forget about putting a
"modern" drive into the box. O.K. you can have an external drive, but the
REAL GOOD THING about the multia is its size. When using an external drive,
I really would recommend a 400/233 Alpha, not a Multia

Chris







