applied) in the middle, no other SCSI-connectors on the cable.
The on board controller is a NCR5c810 (#7).

Problem:
  Suddenly Linux reported a "scsi0 : DAMA FIFO not empty" and than
  "scsi0: unknown command sxfer=0x.. scntl3=0x..".
  These messages appeared many times, sometimes at boot up, then after
  a few minutes. Running "badblocks" on the disk ends up in a couple of
  these messages with total hangup of Linux.

I took the HDD out and put it into a twin machine, *exactly* same
configuration.
Everything was all right, no problems.
When I put back the HDD, I put it to the end of the cable, TermOn, and the
CDROM into the middle. Since then the error didn't occur again.

I've heard of a friend of mine, driving the same basic machine with different
graphic card and hard disk configuration. He has the same problem, but much
stronger: the system hangs at bootup with a SCSI-error.

Any suggestions what the problem was?
And how to avoid it in the future?
Because the system hangs up a real debug is very tricky...

Thanks for your help in advance,
