>as having a CDROM and a Hard drive.
>and memory... im not sure if you an have a SCSI cdrom AND a SCSI hard
>drive also..is there any ways to do this? i only have one scsi connector
>, and im under the impression that its a 50 pin..
>i also believe i have one PCI slot, are there any scsi cards that can
>gimmie another SCSI connector ?
>Is this a good idea? has anyone ever done it? What kind of memory does
>this take, i treid some spare EDO i had laying around, but i got the 14
>blinks of the little green light in the back, i was told that happens
>when the wrong memory is inserted in the slots..I am very interested in
>this new toy.... can someone  help???
>you can email me if more convenient @
>
>dbsaint@ufl.edu
>any comments would be greatly appreciated.. thanx in advance.
>

I can tell you that you need 72-pin TRUE parity RAM, non-EDO for it to
work. (TRUE as in actually parity, not some make believe parity
fudge).

The SCSI contoller is taking up the PCI slot.  If you have an external
SCSI port on your computer, you can connect an external harddrive and
cdrom drive to it.    If you don't have the external port, then there
is a very short cable in the computer in the computer for the
connection to a 3.5" SCSI hard drive (low form factor).  The cable is
soldered onto the SCSI controller so it would be difficult to replace
it with a longer cable.

John Hogan





