Bram Stolk  <bram@nuson.nl> wrote:

>But I do have some problems with my tty:
>vi and 'more', refresh the screen ONLY after
>4 keypresses!!!

This sounds like the tty is not being put into raw mode correctly;
the same byte is used for the EOF character and the MIN value (the first
is applicable in cooked mode, and the second in raw mode). As EOF is
usually ctrl-D (i.e. 4), if this is not changed, the application will
only get keystrokes after there are 4 in the buffer.

Maybe problems with /dev/console / /dev/tty links?

>Anyone else experienced this?

No...


