Yeah... until that battery is replaced, you'll have little or no luck
booting. Mine would occasionally give me a "Clock battery is low... system
may not boot" warning message, but it never said "Yo, your battery is
completely dead, Jack".  It took me a while to figure that out.  It would get
to various points in the boot or ARC console phase of booting and just hang.

One recommendation I would have is to check with your local CD-ROM
hole-in-the- wall store and see if they carry the 6-CD RedHat PowerTools set.
 I got mine for $24 and it has Intel, Alpha (bootable), and SPARC versions of
Redhat 5.1, plus three CD's of goodies.  Made the install a piece of cake. 
Just booted directly from the CD via the SRM console and voila.

> Problem 3:
