Well, that's the correct connector.  I believe it's called a "4 pin Molex"
connector.  I don't have the pinouts, tho (they may be in the Multia service
manual PDF file that's on CPUMicroMart's web page).  You'll probably have a
hard time finding any adapters for it, but I'm certainly not an authority on
that.

A word of warning: the power supply in the Multia is very weak and probably
won't be able to handle anything but a really lightweight internal SCSI drive
with low current requirements.  You're not going to have any luck running a
Seagate Barracuda or anything high-performance unless you put it outside the
box.  I'd be concerned about the heat, too.  My Multia pops popcorn with the
exhaust air.

