Michael Eyrich wrote:

> clock skew of about 6 minutes per hour.
>
> Does anybody know, why?

I don't know why, but I have a suspicion.  Your power mains frequency is
50Hznot 60Hz.  If the system clock is using the mains frequency to
determine the
time, then the difference between this would skew the clock by about 20%
which
would be 12 minutes/hour.  Is there a hardware jumper or software switch
for
specifying the mains frequency?  Or is the clock done entirely with a
single-chip
battery-operated clock that is entirely ignorant of the mains frequency.

Does anyone know if this is a possible explanation?

Bruce





