Hi Guys,

I am finally at a point where I could use some advice. The first thing I
ran into when tried to compile the RADIANCE package (which I have from
the CD in the book, which is an outstanding and exceptional piece of
work BTW) 
was that the librt.a was not built because :

error.c:14: conflicting types for `sys_errlist'
/usr/include/stdio.h:221: previous declaration of `sys_errlist'
make: *** [error.o] Error 1
make: Target `install' not remade because of errors.

To fix this, I out-commented these definition in error.c. The second
thing was the X11 library and include paths, which had to be included in
the rmake command. After that the compilation worked fine. There were a
lot of warning messages though, but everything was where it was supposed
to be.
