directory. The rview interface came up as expected and started refining
the scene but:

make: *** [view] Floating point exception (core dumped)

I tried it the same with the "office" and the "conf" models from the CD
but I always run into this Floating point exception. I played with a few
compiler switches and makeall-install-cleaned the package several times,
but it is always the same message I get and I have seriously no idea how
to get around this error.

My current rmake command is:

#!/bin/sh
exec make "SPECIAL=" \
        "OPT=-O2 -DSPEED=60" \
        "MACH=-DALIGN=double -DBSD -Dlinux -DDCL_ATOF -Dqsort=_quicksort
\
