> internal drive and convenience, or more than one external drive.

Note that there is more than one version of the UDB/Multia.  The one I
have has a riser card with 
 - PCI slot
 - standard 50-pin SCSI header with a ribbon cable attached leading
   to the external port
 - (nonstandard, I assume) more-than-50 pin header leading to the
   internal 2.5" drive
 - what looks like a power header of some kind (4 pins)
 - NCR chip (the SCSI chip).

(having the motherboard and power supply sitting on one's desk,
powered on, facilitates answering hardware questions quite a bit. :)

The model number printed on the underside of the case is VX40B-F2.

The cable going from the riser card to the internal HD does not appear
to be permanently connected, but I'm incapable of testing it right
now.

I believe that there is a model with internal 2.5" drive, PCI slot,
and no external SCSI connector, and a different model (with a
different riser card) with internal 3.5" drive and no PCI slot, but I
don't know if the 3.5" version has an external SCSI connector.

