Joe Duke wrote:

> So, now I have an Alpha with no HDD or CD.  That was yesterday.  Now I have
> a Seagate 2.3GB SCIS drive in it and an external NEC 4exp CD-ROM on it.
> When I boot I get the >>> prompt.
>     NOW WHAT?

This is the SRM console prompt. If you type 'help' you will get the
descriptionof a number of commands. If you type 'show dev' and 'show config'
you
should be able to see what kind of hardware do you have. Armed with this
information this is roughly what you have to do:

1) From another machine where you can read Linux Alpha CDROM and
write a diskette create the MILO image diskette. If you are not sure
of your hardware this can take several trial&error iterations

2) Boot from the diskette with 'boot sda0' (if I remember correctly, check
it anyway with 'show dev').

3) If you have chosen the correct MILO image this will give you a new
console, this time in black and white, from where you can boot Linux (from
the CDROM) and install it.


--
Carlos Vidal
carlos@tarkus.se






