The ARC BIOS is available at 
ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v5.1/alpha200/as200_v6_7.exe

ARC BIOS installation is covered in 
ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/readme/alpha200.html

You need a utility called mkboot.exe to create a bootable disk with the ARC 
BIOS on it. It's available at 

ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/utilities/mkboot.exe

After downloading the as200_v6_7.exe file rename it fwupdate.exe.  Then use 
mkboot to write it to a floppy. (Mkboot gives syntax instructions when you 
invoke it without any other arguments.)

Boot the Alpha to the SRM >> prompt. type boot dva0

The machine will take you to an apu prompt. Type update arc. You'll get 
several easy-to-answer prompts. Type exit when done. Do a cold shutdown. When 
you power back up the machine will come up to an ARC prompt.

To get back to ARC, copy fwupdate.exe (as200_v6_7.exe) to a dos-formatted 
diskette. At the ARC startup screen choose run program --> install new 
firmware. At the apu prompt type update srm.




