Go to the "Console drivers" section off the main configuration menu.
Turn on "Support for frame buffer devices".  Turn on "TGA framebuffer
support".  Turn on "Advanced low level driver options".  Turn on "32
bpp packed pixels support".  This last step is necessary, or you will
get garbage on the screen when you boot.

Don't feel bad.  It took me a week of trial and error to get this
behaving right.

The TGA framebuffer still has some serious problems.  There is a
cursor that always stays on in the lower left hand corner.  Also, the
screen blanking is not working.  All that turns off is the cursor (not
the one in the lower left corner either).  Finally, the frame buffer
appears to cause some screen corruption for the TGA X server.  There
is supposed to be a framebuffer X server out there, but I can't find a
version of it for Alpha.


