dml@b62940.student.cwru.edu (Dave Lukens) writes:

> Would anyone know how to get a multia to use the onboard 10base2 (coax)
> connectoin instead of the AUI or TP?  The machine is running a vanilla
> install of RH5.0.

There exist two network drivers that can be used for the multia
builtin network interface.  From experience with the Debian
installation, I recall that the `tulip' driver does not correctly
autodetect the 10base2 connector.  I had to recompile the kernel using
the `de4x5' driver in order to get this to work.  I don't know whether
this applies to RH5 as well, but if you are seeing bootup messages
indicating that the tulip driver is being used, this is most likely
the cause of your problems.

Hope this helps,
	Alex

