Well, 
I finally got the box up and running with 5.1.  Thanks to Matt
Goheen's post 9/2/98 entitled "Red Hat Linux 5.1 on an AS200 4/233"
which gave me for clues to the magic formula to get MILO to do its
thing, as well as Ron Bacardi for the spiritual support. If you care
about how I was able to get it going read on , if not thanks for
reading this far.

Magical Step:
Copy or x copy noname and linload.exe  from /milo onto a floppy.
Rawrite noname.img to a floppy.
Rawrite ramdisk.img to a floppy.
Make appropriate entries to the Boot menu 

>LOADIDENTIFIER=Linux 
>SYSTEMPARTITION=multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)
>OSLOADER=multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)\linload.exe
>OSLOADPARTITION=multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)
>OSLOADFILENAME=\milo
>OSLOADOPTIONS

Boot Linux with MILO floppy
At MILO> type "boot floppy" with kernel disk in the drive (aka Boot)
Disk.
Then place the RAMDISK when prompted and hopefully you will get the
install screen.

Oscar

 
  



