What worked for me (Alpha server 1000 - Mikasa) is the following
command:

boot dva0 -file vmlinux.gz -flags "load_ramdisk=1 root=/dev/fd0h1440"

Note the "..." to give more than one flag, and the h1440 to force the
kernel
to read a 1.4M disk, and not a 2.8M (as it may think it is...)


Right now I'm stuck at trying to write the bootlx prog on the harddrive.
I would like to be able to boot the thing without playing with a floppy
disk... If anybody has some woodo incantantion to make it work...

