Summary: 

Hello!
After purchasing a 533MHz 164SX system I still have some troubles and solved
one bug ;) Perhaps some other SX164 owners can comment on this or even help
me fixing the problems.
Here is my list:

Floppy DMA still does not work up to kernel 2.1.119
Fix for 2.1.119:
after line 107 of linux/arch/alpha/kernel/sys_sx164.c the follwing two lines
must be added:

static void
sx164_init_irq(void)
{
        outb(0, DMA1_RESET_REG);
        outb(0, DMA2_RESET_REG);
+       outb(DMA_MODE_CASCADE, DMA2_MODE_REG);
+       outb(0, DMA2_MASK_REG);

        if (alpha_using_srm) {


After starting XQuake and beginning a new game system freezes completely
until
mouse is moved, i.e. no ping is answered and all other hw-interrupts seem
not to reach the kernel! Those 'hangs' also occur later in game and
sometimes cause the machine to block completely.

SVGAlib applications crash the machine at once, causing the system to reboot
immediately at startup of SVGAlib application.

Some application cause memory corruptions, like the MPEG-1 video player
'mtvp' from http://www.mpegtv.com/. This runs fine on other Alpha systems!
Memory corruptions are also reported from other applications that use
mmapped files and pthreads. The corruptions cause the application itself to
fail and sometimes causes other unrelated applications to fail too!
Compiling a kernel while playing video for example ends with a sig 11 or
seg-fault.


Any hints welcome!
CU
